    "field": "Paleoclimatology",
    "problem": "The instrumental record of Central Pacific sea-surface temperatures is too short to detect potential long-term trends in El Ni\u00f1o variability, which climate models suggest may be increasing due to rising greenhouse gas concentrations, thus limiting the ability to validate these projections.",
    "method": "An annually resolved reconstruction of NI\u00d1O4 sea-surface temperature is developed using oxygen isotopic time series from Taiwan tree cellulose spanning 1190 to 2007 AD to detect trends in central Pacific El Ni\u00f1o variability over the last eight centuries.",
    "task": "The task is to reconstruct an 818-year history of central Pacific sea-surface temperature using Taiwanese tree-ring oxygen isotopes to investigate whether recent El Ni\u00f1o variability has been enhanced relative to the pre-industrial past.",
    "model": [
        "CMIP5"
